# Frontend Survey Investigation Report — Hark Pro Design System, UI Components, Mascot Decommissioning & Integrations

## 1. Observation

### 1.1 `web/src/styles/tokens.css` (Total Lines: 357)
- **Current Spring Curve (Line 18)**:
  ```css
  --ease-spring: cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);
  ```
  This is a monotonic cubic-bezier without overshoot, directly conflicting with the required 17-point CSS `linear()` spring curve specified in `design.md` (lines 249-251) and R1.
- **Current Palettes (Lines 61-118)**:
  - Lines 61-89: `:root, [data-theme='dark']` uses ad-hoc values:
    ```css
    --bg-from: #000000;
    --bg-to: #060606;
    --card: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
    ```
    Lacks tokens for Hark Pro proactivity tags, verb pills, approval surfaces, specular rim highlights, and explicit squircle geometry radii.
  - Lines 91-118: `[data-theme='light']` uses sky-blue tinted defaults (`--bg-from: #f7fbff; --bg-to: #eaf3fa`) instead of the warm Tactile Alabaster specification.
- **Companion Mascot Styles (Lines 256-336)**:
  Lines 256 through 336 contain the entire `.eyt*` mascot stylesheet:
  - Line 260: `.eyt` (200px frame)
  - Line 266: `.eyt-ball` (with `--eyt-size`)
  - Line 277: `.eyt-body { fill: var(--text); }`
  - Line 279: `.eyt-eye { fill: var(--bg-from); }`
  - Line 286: `.eyt-ball[data-poke]`
  - Line 294: `.eyt-say` (speech bubble)
  - Line 321: `.eyt-caret`
  - Line 328: `@keyframes pet-caret`
  - Line 333: `.eyt-inline .eyt`

### 1.2 Mascot Usage in Layout and Landing
- **`web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx` (Lines 1-25)**:
  - Line 2: `import EyeTracker from '@/components/landing/EyeTracker';`
  - Lines 16-19:
    ```tsx
    <span>Vigil</span>
    <span className="eyt-inline flex items-center" onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}>
      <EyeTracker size={36} shape="Cube" eyes="Slant" eyeScale={1.15} follow={20} bounce={40} within="body" />
    </span>
    ```
- **`web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx` (Lines 80-140)**:
  - Line 23: `import EyeTracker from '@/components/landing/EyeTracker';`
  - Lines 100-111:
    ```tsx
    <span className="text-[15px] font-semibold tracking-heading">Vigil</span>
    <span className="eyt-inline flex items-center">
      <EyeTracker
        size={38}
        shape="Cube"
        eyes="Slant"
        eyeScale={1.15}
        follow={20}
        bounce={40}
        within="body"
      />
    </span>
    ```
- **Vector Spark Primitive**:
  - `web/src/components/chat/MessageItem.tsx` (lines 36-48) already contains the reference 4-point SVG spark:
    ```tsx
    export function VigilSpark({ className = '' }: { className?: string }) {
      return (
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" className={`h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 ${className}`}>
          <path d="M8 1C8.55 4.6 11.4 7.45 15 8C11.4 8.55 8.55 11.4 8 15C7.45 11.4 4.6 8.55 1 8C4.6 7.45 7.45 4.6 8 1Z" />
        </svg>
      );
    }
    ```

### 1.3 Card Shells, Urgency Rails & Verb Buttons
- **`web/src/components/ui/NotificationCard.tsx` (Lines 7-20, 26-75)**:
  - Accepts only `{ avatar, meta, title, children, defaultOpen, bodyId }`.
  - Currently renders `motion.section layout="position" className="card rounded-[18px]"` without an urgency rail, without proactivity tag badges, and without action slot styling.
- **`web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx` (Lines 24-243)**:
  - Lines 121-125: Derives status text and primary action:
    ```tsx
    const [primary, ...rest] = card.actions;
    const isBlocking = card.status === 'awaiting_approval';
    const statusLabel = isBlocking ? 'Waiting on you' : card.due_at ? 'Gentle reminder' : 'For the record';
    ```
  - Lines 195-236: Action button section renders `primary.label` and `rest` labels with generic `.btn-primary` and `.btn-ghost` without proactivity tags or active verb indicators (`verb` field on action).
- **Backend Schema Mapping**:
  - `backend/src/modules/cards/data.py` (lines 18-38): `CardResponse` currently has `urgency: Literal["critical", "high", "medium", "low"]` but lacks `proactivity_tag`.
  - `backend/src/modules/cards/data.py` (lines 8-16): `CardActionSchema` lacks an explicit `verb` field.
  - `web/src/types/index.ts` (lines 19-41): `Card` and `CardAction` match backend but need optional `proactivity_tag?: string | null` and `verb?: string | null`.

### 1.4 Inline Approvals & Chat Flow
- **`web/src/components/chat/InlineApprovalCard.tsx`**:
  - Does NOT exist in codebase currently.
- **`web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx` (Lines 996-1002)**:
  - Currently renders inert static text on `approval_required`:
    ```tsx
    if (item.kind === 'approval_required') {
      return (
        <div className="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-[10px] border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-500/8 px-3 py-2 text-[12px] text-amber-200">
          <span>Waiting on your approval to execute external action</span>
        </div>
      );
    }
    ```
- **`web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx` (Lines 68-74, 90-100)**:
  - Suppresses `ThinkingCapsule` when `chat.awaitingApproval` is true (`showThinking && !chat.awaitingApproval`).
  - Renders a floating button navigating to `/agent/approvals`:
    ```tsx
    {chat.awaitingApproval ? (
      <button onClick={() => navigate('/agent/approvals')} ...>
        The agent is waiting on your approval, open Approvals to decide
      </button>
    ) : null}
    ```
  - However, in `web/src/App.tsx` (lines 90-107), there is NO `/agent/approvals` route registered! Clicking this button navigated to `*` (`/agent`), failing to resolve the approval.
- **Approval Decision API**:
  - `web/src/queries/approvals.ts` (lines 29-49): `useDecideApproval()` is already implemented and calls `api.decideApproval(approvalId, body, scope)`.
  - `backend/src/modules/runs/loop.py` (line 1021): Step `approval_required` emits `payload: {"approval_id": str(approval_id)}`.

### 1.5 Micro-App Previews, Viewport Switcher & Pinned Widgets
- **`web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx` (Lines 19-211, 392-514)**:
  - Supports `markdown`, `pdf`, `docx`, `xlsx`, `csv`, `image`, `html`, `text`.
  - `html` is currently rendered as raw text inside a `<pre>` block (lines 505-508) rather than an interactive sandboxed micro-app preview.
  - Lacks preview/code toggle, lacks viewport switcher (`375px`, `768px`, `100%`), and lacks a pin-to-dashboard affordance.
- **`web/src/components/home/WidgetsRail.tsx` (Lines 48-144)**:
  - Renders Limits card and "Vigil is watching" connector accounts list.
  - Currently lacks a "Pinned Micro-Apps / Widgets" container to display pinned micro-apps from `ArtifactCard`.

### 1.6 Voice Transcription & Connectors Vault/MCP Studio
- **`web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx` (Lines 67-104)**:
  - Currently connects microphone to `AudioContext` and `AnalyserNode` solely for canvas audio wave rendering (`HandoffBeam`).
  - Does NOT capture audio buffers:
    ```tsx
    const stopCapture = () => {
      setRecording(false);
      releaseCapture();
      setNotice('Microphone stopped. Transcription is not connected yet.');
    };
    ```
  - Lacks `MediaRecorder` integration and does not call any transcription endpoint.
- **`web/src/components/settings/sections.tsx` (Lines 266-326)**:
  - `ConnectorsSection` currently renders only a list of `useConnectors()` with a `Refresh` button.
  - Lacks API Key Vault (AES-256-GCM management of `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GROQ_API_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `LINEAR_API_KEY`, custom keys).
  - Lacks 1-click MCP preset gallery (`firecrawl`, `github`, `filesystem`, `postgres`, `linear`).
  - Lacks custom MCP server registration studio (despite `useRegisterMCPServer` and `useUnregisterMCPServer` already existing in `web/src/queries/settings.ts`).

### 1.7 Frontend Build and Verification Commands
- Direct execution test results:
  - `pnpm --prefix web typecheck` -> Exited 0 (`tsc --noEmit`).
  - `pnpm --prefix web build` -> Exited 0 (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`, produced `dist/`).
  - `pnpm --prefix web lint` -> Exited 0 (mapped to `tsc --noEmit` in `package.json`).

---

## 2. Logic Chain

1. **Tokens & Theme Consistency (R1)**:
   - `web/src/styles/tokens.css:18` uses `cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)`. In Tailwind CSS v4, `--ease-spring` under `@theme` defines utility `ease-spring`.
   - Replacing this with the 17-point CSS `linear()` curve (`linear(0, 0.006, 0.025 2.8%, 0.101 6.1%, 0.539 18.9%, 0.721 23.4%, 0.849 28%, 0.937 32.6%, 0.995 37.6%, 1.019 42.2%, 1.026 47.1%, 1.021 54%, 1.001 68.8%, 0.996 82.5%, 1)`) aligns all spring animations with physical specifications.
   - Defining Obsidian Horizon (`[data-theme='dark']`) and Tactile Alabaster (`[data-theme='light']`) variables with squircle radii (`--r-squircle-sm: 18px`, `--r-squircle-md: 20px`, `--r-squircle-lg: 24px`, `--r-squircle-xl: 26px`), specular rim catchlights (`inset 0 1px 0 0 ...`), proactivity tag tokens, and verb pill variables establishes a cohesive Hark Pro foundation.

2. **Complete Mascot Removal (R2)**:
   - Search across `web/src` confirmed that `EyeTracker` is imported only in `HeaderBrand.tsx:2` and `LandingRoute.tsx:23`.
   - Deleting `.eyt*` styles from `tokens.css` (lines 256-336) and replacing `<EyeTracker ... />` with `<VigilSpark />` in `HeaderBrand.tsx` and `LandingRoute.tsx` completely eliminates the mascot artifact while preserving the minimalist `Vigil ✦` brand identity.

3. **Urgency Rails & Verb Pills (R2)**:
   - `TaskCard` renders `NotificationCard`. By adding `urgency` and `proactivityTag` props to `NotificationCard`, `NotificationCard` can render a 3px leading border (`border-l-[3px]`) colored by `--urgency-*` and display the tag badge.
   - `TaskCard` action buttons can display active verbs (`action.verb || action.label`) using `.btn-primary` and `.btn-ghost` styling with squircle geometry.

4. **Inline Approvals Without Navigation (R2)**:
   - `ChatRoute.tsx` previously redirected users to `/agent/approvals` on `chat.awaitingApproval`, which broke because `/agent/approvals` does not exist in `App.tsx`.
   - Creating `InlineApprovalCard.tsx` allows users to view the tool name, arguments, and trigger `decideApproval('approved' | 'rejected')` directly.
   - Mounting `InlineApprovalCard` inside `ThinkingCapsule` on `approval_required` and keeping `ThinkingCapsule` rendered during `chat.awaitingApproval` completes the conversational approval loop seamlessly.

5. **Sandboxed Micro-Apps & Dashboard Pinning (R2)**:
   - In `ArtifactCard.tsx`, HTML/micro-app deliverables can be rendered inside `<iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" srcDoc={content} />`.
   - Adding a code/preview toggle and viewport switcher buttons (`375px`, `768px`, `100%`) provides the required responsive testing canvas.
   - Adding a "Pin to Dashboard" button stores pinned artifacts in a lightweight local store (`useWidgetsStore`), which `WidgetsRail.tsx` reads and renders on the Home surface.

6. **Voice STT & Settings Connectors Studio (R4)**:
   - `InputPill.tsx` already has the microphone lifecycle and audio stream. Attaching `MediaRecorder` to `streamRef.current` allows recording audio chunks on press, generating an audio blob on stop, and sending it to `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe`.
   - `ConnectorsSection` in `sections.tsx` already has access to `useMCPServers`, `useRegisterMCPServer`, and `useUnregisterMCPServer`. Adding the Vault management interface, 1-click Preset Gallery (`firecrawl`, `github`, `filesystem`, `postgres`, `linear`), and Custom Registration Studio delivers the full R4 client suite.

---

## 3. Caveats

- Backend schemas (`backend/src/modules/cards/data.py` and `backend/src/schemas/triage.py`) currently lack `proactivity_tag` and `verb`. The frontend types in `web/src/types/index.ts` should define them as optional (`proactivity_tag?: string | null`, `verb?: string | null`) so frontend works seamlessly in both mock simulation mode and live backend mode.
- In `InputPill.tsx`, `MediaRecorder` requires standard MIME types (`audio/webm` on Chrome/Firefox/Edge, fallback `audio/mp4` on Safari). Fallback mock handling is required so that voice input gracefully produces mock text when the Groq Whisper backend is offline or unconfigured.

---

## 4. Conclusion & Proposed Implementation Specifications

### 4.1 Proposed Tokens in `web/src/styles/tokens.css`
Replace lines 13-23 and lines 56-118 with:
